  "reasoning": "The claim is a well-known myth that is false on multiple levels. According to NASA, astronauts, and optical physics, the Great Wall of China is virtually indistinguishable and not visible to the unaided human eye from low Earth orbit, let alone from the Moon or deeper space, primarily due to its narrow width (rarely exceeding 10 meters) and low contrast with the surrounding terrain. Furthermore, other man-made features—such as major highways, large dams, expansive greenhouse complexes, and city lights at night—are far more visible from low Earth orbit than the Great Wall, meaning it is neither visible with the naked eye nor the 'only' visible human structure.",
